<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <tab id="smaily" translate="label" sortOrder="400">
            <label>Smaily</label>
        </tab>
        <section id="smaily_connect" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="10"
                 showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
            <label>Smaily Connect</label>
            <tab>smaily</tab>
            <resource>Smaily_Connect::config</resource>
            <group id="connection" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>API Connection</label>
                <comment>Connect your Smaily account. You can find API credentials in Smaily under Preferences &gt; API. Credentials can be overridden per website, or per store view for per-language Smaily accounts.</comment>
                <field id="subdomain" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Subdomain</label>
                    <comment>Your Smaily subdomain. For example, if your Smaily URL is https://demo.sendsmaily.net, enter "demo". Pasting the full URL also works.</comment>
                    <backend_model>Smaily\Connect\Model\Config\Backend\Subdomain</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="username" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>API Username</label>
                </field>
                <field id="password" translate="label" type="obscure" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>API Password</label>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Encrypted</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="test_connection" translate="label" type="label" sortOrder="35"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Verify</label>
                    <frontend_model>Smaily\Connect\Block\Adminhtml\Config\TestConnection</frontend_model>
                    <comment>Tests the credentials entered above without saving. Workflow dropdowns below refresh automatically after a successful test.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="multilingual_mode" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="40"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Multilingual Mode</label>
                    <comment>How automation workflows are routed for multi-language stores. Single: one language. Per-language accounts: each store view has its own Smaily account (override credentials at store view scope). Per-language workflows: one account, a workflow per language. Single workflow: one workflow that branches by language inside Smaily.</comment>
                    <source_model>Smaily\Connect\Model\Config\Source\MultilingualMode</source_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="subscribers" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
                <label>Subscriber Synchronization</label>
                <comment>Synchronize newsletter subscribers between this store and Smaily.</comment>
                <field id="sync_enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enable Subscriber Synchronization</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="sync_mode" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Contact Sync Mode</label>
                    <comment>Lawful-basis preset. Subscribers only (default): sync only opted-in newsletter subscribers and mirror Smaily unsubscribes back. All customers (legitimate interest): sync every registered customer; Smaily manages suppression. Checkout opt-in only: no account sync, only customers who tick the checkout checkbox.</comment>
                    <source_model>Smaily\Connect\Model\Config\Source\SyncMode</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="sync_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="sync_fields" translate="label comment" type="multiselect" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Synchronized Fields</label>
                    <comment>Optional customer fields sent to Smaily along with the email address. Empty source values are omitted so existing Smaily values are kept.</comment>
                    <source_model>Smaily\Connect\Model\Config\Source\SyncFields</source_model>
                    <can_be_empty>1</can_be_empty>
                    <depends><field id="sync_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="include_guests" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="40"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Include Guest Order Emails</label>
                    <comment>Also sync emails from guest orders (always on in checkout opt-in mode).</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="sync_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="automation_force_opt_in" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="50"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Automations May Re-Subscribe (Advanced)</label>
                    <comment>Legitimate interest mode only: send force_opt_in on automation triggers, re-subscribing contacts who have unsubscribed in Smaily. Leave off to honour unsubscribes (GDPR Art. 21).</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="sync_mode">legitimate_interest</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="checkout_optin_enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="55"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Show Newsletter Checkbox At Checkout</label>
                    <comment>Adds a newsletter opt-in checkbox to the checkout payment step. Works for both guests and registered customers.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="suppress_optin_emails" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="60"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Let Smaily Send Opt-In Emails</label>
                    <comment>Suppress Magento's own newsletter confirmation and unsubscription emails so Smaily automations handle them instead.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="automations" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
                <label>Automations</label>
                <comment>Trigger Smaily automation workflows on store events. Workflow lists load from your Smaily account after the API connection is saved. In per-language multilingual modes, per-language workflow mappings override these defaults.</comment>
                <field id="welcome_enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enable Welcome Automation</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="welcome_workflow" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Welcome Workflow</label>
                    <source_model>Smaily\Connect\Model\Config\Source\Workflows</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="welcome_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="first_order_enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enable First Order Automation</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="first_order_workflow" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="40"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
                    <label>First Order Workflow</label>
                    <source_model>Smaily\Connect\Model\Config\Source\Workflows</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="first_order_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="abandoned_enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="50"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enable Abandoned Cart Automation</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="abandoned_workflow" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="60"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Abandoned Cart Workflow</label>
                    <source_model>Smaily\Connect\Model\Config\Source\Workflows</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="abandoned_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="abandoned_cutoff" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="70"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Abandoned Cart Cutoff (Minutes)</label>
                    <comment>How long a cart must be inactive before it counts as abandoned. Minimum 10 minutes. Carts older than 24 hours are never mailed.</comment>
                    <validate>validate-digits digits-range-10-1440</validate>
                    <depends><field id="abandoned_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="abandoned_fields" translate="label comment" type="multiselect" sortOrder="80"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Abandoned Cart Product Fields</label>
                    <comment>Product data included for up to 10 cart items (product_name_1..10 etc.).</comment>
                    <source_model>Smaily\Connect\Model\Config\Source\AbandonedFields</source_model>
                    <can_be_empty>1</can_be_empty>
                    <depends><field id="abandoned_enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="engine_automations" translate="label" type="label" sortOrder="100"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label/>
                    <frontend_model>Smaily\Connect\Block\Adminhtml\Config\EngineAutomations</frontend_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="rss" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Product RSS Feed</label>
                <comment><![CDATA[The product feed for the Smaily template editor is served at <strong>{store URL}smaily/rss/feed</strong>. Optional query parameters: <em>category</em> (category ID), <em>limit</em> (1-250, default 50), <em>sort</em> (created_at, updated_at, name, price), <em>order</em> (asc, desc). Example: https://example.com/smaily/rss/feed?category=12&limit=100&sort=updated_at]]></comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enable RSS Feed</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="intelligence" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="50"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Campaign Intelligence</label>
                <comment>Optional integration with the Smaily recommendation engine: catalog, customer, order and browse data power personalized recommendations and engine-run automations.</comment>
                <field id="status" translate="label" type="label" sortOrder="5"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Connection Status</label>
                    <frontend_model>Smaily\Connect\Block\Adminhtml\Config\EngineStatus</frontend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="setup_token" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Setup Token or URL</label>
                    <comment>Paste the one-time setup URL (or token) provided by Smaily and save the configuration to connect. The token is exchanged immediately and never stored.</comment>
                    <backend_model>Smaily\Connect\Model\Config\Backend\EngineSetupToken</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="sync_catalog" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Sync Catalog</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="sync_customers" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Sync Customers</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="sync_orders" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="40"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Sync Orders</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="browse_tracking" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="50"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Storefront Browse Tracking</label>
                    <comment>Sends anonymized browsing events (product views, searches, cart activity) to the engine. Respects Magento cookie restriction mode. Off by default.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="logging" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="900"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Logging</label>
                <field id="verbosity" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Log Verbosity</label>
                    <comment>Logs are written to var/log/smaily_connect.log. Debug verbosity logs full API requests and responses; use only for troubleshooting.</comment>
                    <source_model>Smaily\Connect\Model\Config\Source\LogVerbosity</source_model>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
